  "body": "### Description\n\nThis is an editorial and infrastructure maintenance pull request addressing several bugs and security considerations across specification helper scripts, styles, and demos:\n\n- **`html-dfn.js`**: Grouped `storage` inside the regex alternation and removed the trailing empty pipe (`|/`), which previously matched empty strings and prepended empty `<code></code>` tags before every reference title.\n- **`link-fixup.js`**: Guarded `fragid` fragment lookup using `Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty` to avoid prototype property matches (e.g., `#toString`), safely decoded the hash inside a `try...catch` to avoid uncaught `URIError` on malformed percent encoding, and replaced deprecated `substr()` with `slice()`.\n- **`dev/search.js`**: Replaced dynamic regex creation with safe case-insensitive substring search to prevent uncaught `SyntaxError` crashes when users type regex characters (`(`, `[`, `*`, etc.); added HTML entity escaping and URL encoding to avoid injection; updated keyboard navigation to traverse element siblings instead of whitespace text nodes; and guarded the `/` search shortcut from stealing focus while typing in inputs.\n- **`styles.css`**: Corrected selector typo from `#table-import-map-scopes-example th[row=\"3\"]`, which never matched, to `th[rowspan=\"3\"]`, restoring the intended `writing-mode: vertical-rl` on the Referrer table header.\n- **`demos/workers/crypto/libcrypto-v2.js`**: Renamed duplicate `function encrypt(p)` definition to `function decrypt(p)` so the decryptor worker can be reached and doesn't overwrite encrypt.\n- **`demos/canvas/blue-robot/*.html`**: Replaced non-standard `context.lineStyle` with standard `context.strokeStyle`.\n- **`demos/workers/multiviewer/worker.js`**: Corrected inverted row/column coordinate boundaries in `sendMapData` and `wrapY`, and guarded `viewers` lookup against prototype keys.\n- **`var-click-highlighting.js`**: Added null safety to the DOM traversal loop to prevent `Cannot read properties of null` errors.\n- **`source`**: Added contributor to the Acknowledgments list lexicographically.\n\nThis is a Meta/editorial maintenance PR (no normative spec changes).\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13073/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 14, 2026, 10:57 AM UTC (5d90f62)\">/acknowledgements.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13073/790ce89...5d90f62/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 14, 2026, 10:57 AM UTC (5d90f62)\">diff</a> )",
